4	-- Fixes all Supabase database linter warnings:
5	--
6	--   1. search_path mutable  — every function in public schema gets
7	--      SET search_path = public so it cannot be tricked by a schema
8	--      injection attack.
9	--
10	--   2. RLS policies always true — stub tables that previously had a
11	--      blanket FOR ALL … USING (true) WITH CHECK (true) policy are
12	--      replaced with:
13	--        • SELECT: USING (true)  — reads are still open (stubs are empty)
14	--        • INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE: WITH CHECK / USING (auth.uid() IS NOT NULL)
15	--          — writes require an authenticated session
16	--
17	-- ============================================================================
18	
19	
20	-- ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
21	-- PART 1: Fix search_path on every function in the public schema
22	-- ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
23	-- Using ALTER FUNCTION … SET search_path = public is the recommended fix.
24	-- Each statement targets the exact argument signature as declared in the
25	-- originating migration so PostgreSQL can resolve overloaded names correctly.
26	
